{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/ActorSystem-swift.associatedtype","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/SerializationRequirement"],"title":"Associated Types","generated":true,"anchor":"Associated-Types"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/init(from:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/actorSystem-swift.property","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/asLocalActor","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/id","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/unownedExecutor"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/assertIsolated(_:file:line:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/assumeIsolated(_:file:line:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/encode(to:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/preconditionIsolated(_:file:line:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/whenLocal(_:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/resolve(id:using:)"],"title":"Type Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DistributedActor","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : AnyObject, ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s12IdentifiableP","text":"Identifiable","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Identifiable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DistributedActor"},{"text":" protocol generalizes over all distributed actor types.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Distributed actor types implicitly conform to this protocol.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is not possible to conform to this protocol by any other declaration other than a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distributed actor"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is possible to require a type to conform to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol by refining it with another protocol,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or by using a generic constraint.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Synthesized-properties","type":"heading","text":"Synthesized properties"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For every concrete distributed actor declaration, the compiler synthesizes two properties: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actorSystem"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They witness the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/actorSystem-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/id"},{"text":" protocol requirements of the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor"},{"text":" protocol.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is not possible to implement these properties explicitly in user code."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"These properties are "},{"code":"nonisolated","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and accessible even if the instance is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"remote"}]},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"all","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" distributed actor references must store the actor system remote calls"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"will be delivered through, as well as the id identifying the target of those calls."}]},{"anchor":"The-ActorSystem-associated-type","text":"The ActorSystem associated type","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every distributed actor must declare what type of actor system","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it is part of by implementing the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/ActorSystem-swift.associatedtype","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" associated type requirement."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This causes a number of other properties of the actor to be inferred:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/SerializationRequirement"},{"type":"text","text":" that will be used at compile time to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"verify "},{"code":"distributed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" target declarations are well formed,"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"if the distributed actor is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", based on the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" being Codable or not,","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"the type of the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/ActorSystem-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":" accepted in the synthesized default initializer.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A distributed actor must declare what type of actor system it is ready to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"work with by fulfilling the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/ActorSystem-swift.associatedtype","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" type member requirement:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["distributed actor Greeter {","  typealias ActorSystem = GreetingSystem \/\/ which conforms to DistributedActorSystem","","  func greet() -> String { \"Hello!\" }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"The-DefaultDistributedActorSystem-type-alias","text":"The DefaultDistributedActorSystem type alias","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since it is fairly common to only be using one specific type of actor system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"within a module or entire codebase, it is possible to declare the default type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of actor system all distributed actors will be using in a module by declaring"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultDistributedActorSystem"},{"type":"text","text":" module wide typealias:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Distributed","import AmazingActorSystemLibrary","","typealias DefaultDistributedActorSystem = AmazingActorSystem","","distributed actor Greeter {} \/\/ ActorSystem == AmazingActorSystem"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This declaration makes all "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distributed actor"},{"type":"text","text":" declarations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that do not explicitly specify an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/ActorSystem-swift.associatedtype"},{"type":"text","text":" type alias to assume the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmazingActorSystem"},{"type":"text","text":" as their "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ActorSystem"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is possible for a specific actor to override the system it is using,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by declaring an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/ActorSystem-swift.associatedtype"},{"type":"text","text":" type alias as usual:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["typealias DefaultDistributedActorSystem = AmazingActorSystem","","distributed actor Amazing {","  \/\/ ActorSystem == AmazingActorSystem","}","","distributed actor Superb {","  typealias ActorSystem = SuperbActorSystem","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In general the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultDistributedActorSystem"},{"type":"text","text":" should not be declared public,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as picking the default should be left up to each specific module of a project."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Default-initializer","text":"Default initializer","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"While classes and actors receive a synthesized ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"argument-free default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"initializer","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"text":"), distributed actors synthesize a default initializer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that accepts a distributed actor system the actor is part of: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(actorSystem:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The accepted actor system must be of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self.ActorSystem"},{"text":" type, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must conform to the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActorSystem","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol. This is required","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because distributed actors are always managed by a concrete","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"distributed actor system and cannot exist on their own without one.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is possible to explicitly declare a parameter-free initializer (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"however the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actorSystem"},{"type":"text","text":" property still must be assigned a concrete actor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system instance the actor shall be part of."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In general it is recommended to always have an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actorSystem"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the last non-defaulted non-closure parameter in every actor’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"initializer parameter list. This way it is simple to swap in a “test actor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system” instance in unit tests, and avoid relying on global state which could"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"make testing more difficult."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Implicit-properties","text":"Implicit properties","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every concrete "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distributed actor"},{"type":"text","text":" type receives two synthesized properties,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which implement the protocol requirements of this protocol: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actorSystem"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Property-Actor-System","text":"Property: Actor System","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/actorSystem-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":" property is an important part of every distributed actor’s lifecycle management."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both initialization as well as de-initialization require interactions with the actor system,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and it is the actor system that handles all remote interactions of an actor, by both sending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or receiving remote calls made on the actor."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/actorSystem-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":" property must be assigned in every designated initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of a distributed actor explicitly. It is highly recommended to make it a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parameter of every distributed actor initializer, and simply forward the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value to the stored property, like this:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["init(name: String, actorSystem: Self.ActorSystem) {","  self.name = name","  self.actorSystem = actorSystem","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Forgetting to initialize the actor system, will result in a compile time error:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ BAD","init(name: String, actorSystem: Self.ActorSystem) {","  self.name = name","  \/\/ BAD, will cause compile-time error; the `actorSystem` was not initialized.","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Property-Distributed-Actor-Identity","text":"Property: Distributed Actor Identity","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" is assigned by the actor system during the distributed actor’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"initialization, and cannot be set or mutated by the actor itself.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/id"},{"text":" is the effective identity of the actor, and is used in equality checks,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as well as the actor’s synthesized ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance if the "},{"code":"ID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"conforms to "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Automatic Conformances","anchor":"Automatic-Conformances","type":"heading"},{"level":3,"text":"Hashable and Identifiable conformance","anchor":"Hashable-and-Identifiable-conformance","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every distributed actor conforms to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable"},{"text":" protocols.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Its identity is strictly driven by its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/id","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and therefore hash and equality"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"implementations directly delegate to the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/id"},{"text":" property.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Comparing a local distributed actor instance and a remote reference to it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(both using the same "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/id"},{"type":"text","text":") always returns true, as they both conceptually"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point at the same distributed actor."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is not possible to implement these protocols relying on the actual actor’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state, because it may be remote and the state may not be available. In other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"words, since these protocols must be implemented using ","type":"text"},{"code":"nonisolated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" functions,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only ","type":"text"},{"code":"nonisolated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"actorSystem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" properties are accessible for their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"implementations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Implicit Codable conformance","anchor":"Implicit-Codable-conformance","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If created with an actor system whose "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActorSystem\/ActorID"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compiler will synthesize code for the concrete distributed actor to conform"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as well."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is necessary to support distributed calls where the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SerializationRequirement"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and thus users may want to pass actors as arguments to remote calls."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The synthesized implementations use a single "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SingleValueEncodingContainer"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encode\/decode the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor\/id"},{"text":" property of the actor. The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Decoder"},{"text":" required","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Decoder\/init(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is implemented by retrieving an actor system from the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"decoders’ ","type":"text"},{"code":"userInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", effectively like as follows:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["decoder.userInfo[.actorSystemKey] as? ActorSystem","","The such obtained actor system is then used to ``resolve(id:using:)`` the decoded ``ID``.","","Use the ``CodingUserInfoKey\/actorSystemKey`` to provide the necessary","actor system for the decoding initializer when decoding a distributed actor.","","- SeeAlso: ``DistributedActorSystem``","- SeeAlso: ``Actor``","- SeeAlso: ``AnyActor``"]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Equatable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Hashable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Identifiable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sendable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SendableMetatype"],"title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/distributed\/distributedactor"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActor"},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DistributedActor","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DistributedActor","role":"symbol","platforms":[{"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,